Appendix B: Decision Rules and Formula Compendium

B.1 R Aggregation Rule (Crisp)

R = 1 \iff (z_{D1} > P_{90,D1}) \land (z_{D2} > P_{90,D2}) \land (z_{D3} > P_{90,D3}) \land (z_{D4} > P_{90,D4}) 

where z_{Di} is the z‑score of dimension i, and P_{90,Di} is the 90th percentile of that dimension within the polity‑period sample.

B.2 HERI Aggregation Rule
Sub‑indices:

· HERI‑A (Availability): 0–3 (number of independent source genres).
· HERI‑I (Independence): ordinal (high, medium, low).
· HERI‑C (Consistency): ordinal (high, medium, low).

Overall HERI rating (conjunctive):

· High reliability: HERI‑A ≥ 2 ∧ HERI‑I = high ∧ HERI‑C = high.
· Moderate reliability: all three sub‑indices ≥ medium ∧ at least one high.
· Low reliability: any sub‑index = low.
· Insufficient evidence: HERI‑A = 0 or all sub‑indices missing.

B.3 FTC Composite

\text{FTC} = z\left( z(\text{FT1}) + z(\text{FT2}) + z(\text{FT3}) + z(\text{FT4}) \right) 

where each z(\text{FTi}) is a z‑score within the polity‑period sample.

B.4 DAD Dimensions

\text{DAD-H} = \frac{ z(\text{H1}) + z(\text{H2}) + z(\text{H3}) + z(\text{H4}) }{4} 

\text{DAD-U} = \frac{ z(\text{U1}) + z(\text{U2}) + z(\text{U3}) + z(\text{U4}) }{4} 

No single DAD total is computed.

B.5 Alliance Instability Rate

\text{P-AI}_{\text{raw}} = \frac{\text{number of alliance breaks}}{\text{years from first political engagement to accession}} 

\text{P-AI} = \text{P-AI}_{\text{raw}} - \overline{\text{P-AI}_{\text{raw}}}(\text{elite comparison cohort}) 

B.6 Institutional Trajectory

\Delta I_{\text{formal}} = I_{\text{formal}}(t+1) - I_{\text{formal}}(t-5) 

Negative values indicate post‑accession decline.

B.7 Fuzzy‑Set Calibration for QCA
For all conditions (FTC, DAD‑H, DAD‑U, P‑DT, P‑AI, P‑BF1, P‑BF2, S1, S2, S3, I_formal(t‑5), ΔI_formal, I_informal(t‑5)):

· Full membership threshold: 95th percentile of the sample distribution.
· Crossover point: 50th percentile (median).
· Full non‑membership threshold: 5th percentile.
  For R: thresholds as above for the four dimensions, then R_fuzzy = min(μ_D1, μ_D2, μ_D3, μ_D4).

