Appendix D: Formal Statement of Theoretical Expectations with Falsification Criteria

All expectations are directional until pre‑registered numeric thresholds are specified. A worked example is provided for Expectation 3.

Expectation 1 (Developmental Conjunction):
The tyrannical regime pattern R is probabilistically associated with the conjunction of high FTC, high DAD‑H, high DAD‑U, high P‑DT, high P‑AI, and high S (dominance‑reinforcing). The effect of any single factor in isolation is expected to be weak or null.
Proposed pre‑registered threshold (example): In a logistic regression, the interaction term FTC × DAD‑H × P‑DT must have OR > 2.0 and 95% CI excluding 1.0, controlling for I_formal(t‑5) and C.
QCA criterion: The configuration [FTC ≥ 0.8] · [DAD‑H ≥ 0.8] · [DAD‑U ≥ 0.8] · [P‑DT ≥ 0.8] · [S ≥ 0.8] must achieve consistency ≥ 0.85 as a sufficient condition for R_fuzzy ≥ 0.8, with coverage > 0.5.

Expectation 2 (Institutional Moderation):
Under conditions of high I_formal(t‑5) (top tercile of the sample) AND high I_informal(t‑5) (top tercile), the developmental profile variables will not significantly predict R (p > 0.10 for the main effect of the profile composite).

Expectation 3 (Institutional Decline Amplification):
The interaction term (high‑risk profile × ΔI_formal) is positive and significant. This amplification is stronger for Pathway A (endogenous dismantling) and Pathway C (accelerated exogenous decline) than for Pathway B (purely exogenous collapse).

Worked falsification criterion (provisional):

· In a logistic regression of R on high‑risk profile indicator (binary, top quartile of FTC+DAD+P composite), ΔI_formal, and their interaction: the coefficient on the interaction term must be positive with 95% CI excluding zero.
· When cases are split by process‑tracing pathway coding:
  · The interaction coefficient for Pathway A must be at least 50% larger in magnitude than that for Pathway B.
  · The interaction coefficient for Pathway C must be positive and its 95% CI must exclude zero.
  · The Pathway B coefficient’s 95% CI may include zero without falsifying the theory.

Expectation 4 (Civilisational Moderation):
Only cases where the human‑cost dimension (D2) exceeds the civilisation‑century 90th percentile are classified as R = 1 for that dimension. Using absolute modern thresholds should substantially alter the set of classified cases (kappa < 0.70 expected).

Expectation 5 (Dominance–Prestige Clustering):
In the 2×2 space (coerciveness × state‑building orientation), the tyrannical regime pattern forms a distinct cluster in the high‑coercion, high‑state‑building quadrant. Cluster analysis (e.g., k‑means with k = 4) should recover this quadrant as a distinct cluster, with silhouette width > 0.5.

Configurational truth table (QCA):
Future QCA analysis will construct a truth table with the following conditions (all calibrated as fuzzy sets): FTC, DAD‑H, DAD‑U, P‑DT (composite), P‑AI, S (composite), I_formal(t‑5), ΔI_formal, I_informal(t‑5). The outcome is R_fuzzy. The analysis will test whether the row corresponding to [all developmental and social conditions high, I_formal(t‑5) low, ΔI_formal negative, I_informal(t‑5) low] is a consistent sufficient condition for R (consistency ≥ 0.85). Robustness checks will vary calibration thresholds and minimum case frequency.

